course: dictionary
lesson: 11010
title: How a waterfall is made
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A waterfall is a place where a river or stream flows over the edge of a cliff or steep rock and falls down. Look at the clues: the water pours over an edge and drops, so it is not just a fast river on flat ground.
explain: Context shows how waterfalls form. «Where it pours over a band of hard rock lying on soft rock, the soft rock wears back faster and a waterfall forms.» The words hard, soft and wears show the rock changing over time. Swap in your meaning to check: a waterfall forms where water wears away soft rock under hard rock.
explain: Fish and animals use waterfalls too. «Atlantic salmon ... can leap over 3 metres to climb waterfalls.» The word leap tells you a salmon jumps up the falls. When context is not enough, a dictionary or a teacher can settle it.
fact: A waterfall is where a river or stream flows over the edge of a cliff or steep rock and falls down.
fact: Waterfalls form where a river flows over hard rock lying on softer rock; the soft rock wears away faster, a step and a plunge pool form, and the waterfall slowly moves back upstream.
fact: Angel Falls is the highest of the famous waterfalls.
fact: Falling water can be used to make electricity.
fact: Rocks near waterfalls are slippery, so always stay behind the barriers.
exercise: «Waterfalls form where a river flows over hard rock lying on top of softer rock.» Which rock wears away faster? | Hard rock | Neither rock ever wears away | Both wear away at exactly the same speed | *Soft rock
exercise: What is a waterfall? | A quiet pond in a wood | A kind of fish that leaps | A mountain made of ice | *A place where a river or stream flows over a cliff or steep rock and falls down
exercise: «Atlantic salmon can leap over 3 metres to climb waterfalls.» What does leap mean? | Hatch from an egg | Swim very slowly | Sleep under the water | *Jump up into the air
test: Rocks near waterfalls are slippery. What should you do near a waterfall? | Climb to the top to see better | *Stay behind the barriers | Swim right up to the edge | Slide down the wet rocks
test: «The waterfall slowly moves back upstream.» What does upstream mean? | Across the river | Downhill towards the sea | Under the ground | *Towards where the river starts
exam: «Where it pours over a band of hard rock lying on soft rock, the soft rock wears back faster and a waterfall forms.» What happens to the soft rock? | It turns into hard rock | It stays exactly the same | *It wears away faster | It grows taller
